BEFORE:

At the end of the day, This was the home of Henry Jekyll’s favourite;

AFTER:

This was the home of Henry Jekyll’s favourite;

SURROUNDING PARAGRAPH:

As the cab drew up before the address indicated, the fog lifted a little and showed him a dingy street, a gin palace, a low French eating house, a shop for the retail of penny numbers and twopenny salads, many ragged children huddled in the doorways, and many women of many different nationalities passing out, key in hand, to have a morning glass; and the next moment the fog settled down again upon that part, as brown as umber, and cut him off from his blackguardly surroundings. At the end of the day, This was the home of Henry Jekyll’s favourite; of a man who was heir to a quarter of a million sterling.

